# Prompt 1.5 — CRM V4 Component Standards

The Design Tokens have already been implemented.

From this point forward, every component created for the CRM V4 Design System must follow the same visual language.

These rules become the default for every future component unless explicitly overridden by a Figma or design reference.

---

# Design Philosophy

The CRM V4 is a professional enterprise system.

The visual language should be closer to:

- HubSpot
- Linear
- Atlassian
- Notion
- Stripe Dashboard

Avoid the exaggerated rounded appearance commonly found in many Tailwind examples.

Components should feel:

- professional
- clean
- dense
- consistent
- enterprise
- timeless

---

# Radius Rules

Use these values consistently.

## Form Controls

Input
Select
Textarea
Combobox
DatePicker
Button

→ rounded-md (~6px)

Never use:

rounded-xl
rounded-2xl

---

## Floating Components

Popover
Dropdown
Context Menu
Command
Tooltip

→ rounded-lg (~8px)

---

## Containers

Card
Dialog
Drawer
Calendar
Table containers

→ rounded-lg (~10px)

---

## Pills

Badge
Tag
Status

→ rounded-full

---

## Avatars

Always fully circular.

---

# Density

Prefer medium density.

Avoid oversized paddings.

Good enterprise density is preferred over "marketing website" spacing.

---

# Typography

Prefer:

- medium hierarchy
- semibold titles
- regular body
- muted descriptions

Avoid oversized headings.

---

# Shadows

Only use semantic shadows.

Cards:

shadow-card

Floating:

shadow-dropdown

Dialogs:

shadow-modal

---

# Borders

Borders should be subtle.

Prefer:

border-border

Avoid thick outlines.

---

# Buttons

Buttons should have:

- compact radius
- balanced horizontal padding
- consistent heights

Support:

Primary

Secondary

Outline

Ghost

Link

Success

Warning

Danger

Icon Button

Loading

Disabled

Button Group

Split Button

Toolbar examples

---

# Inputs

Every input family should demonstrate:

Default

Disabled

Readonly

Error

Success

Loading

Prefix

Suffix

Search

Clear Button

Validation

Real CRM examples

---

# Tables

Every table family should demonstrate:

Loading

Empty

Error

Selection

Sorting

Filtering

Pagination

Bulk Actions

Expandable

Responsive

---

# Component Families

Do not create isolated components.

Every component should represent a complete family.

Examples:

Button

Input

Card

Dialog

Calendar

Table

Badge

Toast

Chart

Combobox

Tooltip

Tabs

Each family should include every variant naturally expected for an enterprise CRM.

---

# Styleguide Rules

The Styleguide is the official approval environment.

Every component page must include:

Overview

Variants

Sizes

States

Dark Mode

Accessibility

Composition

Real CRM examples

Responsive examples

Code examples

API

Best Practices

Do / Don't

---

# Visual Consistency

Every component must look like it belongs to the same ecosystem.

A user should never be able to tell which component came from shadcn and which one was custom-built.

Everything should feel like one cohesive Design System.

---

# Future Components

All future components automatically inherit these standards.

No additional confirmation is required unless a Figma explicitly overrides these rules.